@@ -41,6 +41,14 @@ resolves the caller's membership; a caller who is not a member gets 404 for the
 if it did not exist. Whoever creates an organisation becomes its first owner, and an organisation
 always keeps at least one owner.
 
+An owner hands the organisation over with `POST /v1/orgs/{org_id}/transfer-ownership
+{"user_id": …, "stay_owner": false}`: the member named becomes an owner and the caller becomes an
+admin, or stays an owner with `"stay_owner": true`. Only a member whose own role is `owner` may
+transfer (holding `org:manage` through a role assignment is not enough); the new owner must
+already be a member, enabled, and not an owner yet. Both changes happen in one transaction under
+the organisation lock, role assignments are left alone, and the audit log gets a
+`member.role_changed` event per changed membership plus `org.ownership_transferred`.
+
 **Roles and permissions.** Permissions are strings of the form `resource:action`:
 
 | Permission | Grants |
